      "explanation": "[NiCl<sub>4</sub>]<sup>2–</sup> : Oxidation state of Ni in [NiCl<sub>4</sub>]<sup>2–</sup> = + 2 \n<br><img src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1qpqdn5k7ttyawf/7ca5f4de-1d50-4190-ac7b-dcf4298293fc/357ab3f0-672b-11ea-997e-790b4402a570/file-1qpqdn5k7ttyawg-320w.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%;height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Main 2018 (Online) 15th April Morning Slot Chemistry - Coordination Compounds Question 313 English Explanation 1\">\n<br><br>Cl<sup>–</sup> is a weak field ligand and cannot take part in pairing of electrons.\n<img src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1qpqdn5k7tu0z9z/03fb57bd-d795-4405-9daa-2857070448b5/7fed8a70-672b-11ea-997e-790b4402a570/file-1qpqdn5k7tu0za0-320w.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%;height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Main 2018 (Online) 15th April Morning Slot Chemistry - Coordination Compounds Question 313 English Explanation 2\">\n<br>Hence, the complex is tetrahedral and paramagnetic with two unpaired electrons.\n<br><br>[Ni(CO)<sub>4</sub>] : Oxidation state of Ni in [Ni(CO)<sub>4</sub>] is zero. CO is a strong field ligand thus pairing of electrons takes place in d-orbitals.\n<img src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1qpqdn5k7tu3zqf/28558019-35cb-4298-a1cf-5557c989fdb3/d3b54b70-672b-11ea-997e-790b4402a570/file-1qpqdn5k7tu3zqg-320w.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%;height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Main 2018 (Online) 15th April Morning Slot Chemistry - Coordination Compounds Question 313 English Explanation 3\">\n<br>Hence, the complex is tetrahedral and diamagnetic."
